        <!-- ===== 04 · CERTIFICATE · FAB · TABLE D "LAB REPORT" ===== -->
        <section id="certificate" class="sec">
          <h2>What Is Printed on a Real DNA Sexing Certificate?</h2>
          <p class="opener">Nobody on the first page of results for this search shows you one, so the phrase "certificate included" does a great deal of unexamined work in this market. A real certificate is a short, dull document with seven fields on it, and every one of those fields exists so that somebody can check something. Below is the whole anatomy, field by field, with what each line is for.</p>
          <img class="sec-img inf-img" src={IMG + "anatomy-of-a-dna-sexing-certificate.webp"} srcset={IMG + "anatomy-of-a-dna-sexing-certificate-760.webp 760w, " + IMG + "anatomy-of-a-dna-sexing-certificate.webp 1408w"} sizes="(max-width:900px) 92vw, 760px" width="1408" height="768" loading="lazy" alt="Diagram of the fields a legitimate avian DNA sexing certificate carries, including band number, species, method and result" />
          <p class="cap">An explanatory diagram of the fields, not a scan of our paperwork — the value bars are deliberately blank.</p>

          <h3>The Fields Every Legitimate Certificate Carries</h3>
          <div class="tblwrap">
            <table class="tblD">
              <caption class="tblD-cap">Lab Report — anatomy of an avian DNA sexing certificate</caption>
              <thead><tr><th scope="col">Field</th><th scope="col">What it holds</th><th scope="col">Why the field exists</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                {certFields.map((r, i) => (
                  <tr>
